Independent conceptual inspiration
-----------------------------------

DigitalEuan/GLM — Geometric Language Machine
https://github.com/DigitalEuan/GLM
Author: Euan R. A. Craig (DigitalEuan)

Conceptual inspiration reviewed during the NEXUS 2.x architecture discussion:
persistent growth across sessions, a substrate-native cognitive environment,
model/world separation questions, sandbox experimentation, and durable learned
state. NEXUS 2.x does not copy GLM source code; it takes a different
model-independent approach in which heterogeneous cognitive actors inhabit one
shared world through replaceable adapters.

Edward de Bono / parallel thinking
----------------------------------

The NEXUS Council phase sequence is conceptually inspired by Edward de Bono's
well-known Six Thinking Hats / parallel-thinking method. NEXUS adapts the idea
of having all participants move through common thinking modes (White, Red,
Black, Yellow, Green, Blue) for a machine Council protocol. No proprietary
training material or third-party implementation is included.

Provider names
--------------

OpenAI, Anthropic/Claude, Google/Gemini, xAI/Grok, Ollama and other provider or
model names may appear in architecture examples solely to describe planned
adapter interoperability. NEXUS is not endorsed by those providers and grants
no provider special authority inside a Council.

